<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105460" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίχωρος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with three
				divisions</i> or <i>cells,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.101
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίχωρον, τό,</span> wine measure in Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				248.26
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>tricorus vel trichorus locus prandii qui et sima</i> (i. e.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίγμα</span>) <i>dicitur; trichorum
				sive trichorium locus prandii; tricora tres cameras sive tres
				absidas,</i> all in <u>Gloss.</u>
        </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
